  "lesson": "## Same alphabet, other hand\n\n\n  Start on the C one octave below middle C with your pinky. Fingering going up: 5 4 3 2 1, then cross the 3rd finger over the thumb, 3 2 1. Coming down: 1 2 3, tuck the thumb under to 1, 2 3 4 5.\n\n\n  The left hand feels weaker because it is. Play at a tempo where every note is even in volume, and drop the tempo slider until that is true.\n",
